Kubernetes Service types 


How do you let people reach your app? It depends on who you want to let in.

 - ClusterIP

A private IP inside the cluster. Use it when only other services in the cluster need to reach your app.

 - NodePort

Exposes your Service on a port (30000 to 32767) on every node in the cluster. Handy for testing.

- LoadBalancer

Creates a cloud load balancer with an external IP, usually public. Useful, but one for every Service gets expensive fast.

 Common production approach

Instead of giving every Service its own LoadBalancer, use an Ingress with an Ingress Controller. One entry point routes traffic to many applications:

User → Load Balancer → Ingress Controller → Service → Pod
